--- body ---
## Context
A hook that runs when an agent ends its turn, on Claude Code, Codex and Pi, to observe and later refuse two bad stops: a question to the author with no ask-up, and a wait with nothing tracked to wake the agent. Design, reviews and plan: `conception/2026-10-21-stopguard-design.md` (reviewed by Fable, Astra and a KISS pass). The end-of-turn mechanism was smoke-tested headless on all three harnesses on 2026-10-21.

Deferred by the author on 2026-10-21: no implementation, and no phase 1 work, until the deferral is lifted. Children are filed when it is lifted, not before.

Related: the waiter that gives rule 2 a pass condition is designed in another session (`conception/discussions/2026-10-21-await-external-design.md` on branch `explore-await-external-*`, uncommitted). It owns the wait registry; this tracker owns the only Stop-hook implementation.

## Children (to file at lift time, one sign-off unit each)
- phase 1: close the design's smoke gaps; runner, two rules, dry only, spool, three adapters (3.5 agent h, 0.3 author h)
- phase 2: weekly report and git-visible report path (0.5, 0.25)
- phase 3: Claude Code replay harness; gate G1 (2, 0.25)
- phase 3b: Codex and Pi replay, after G1 (1.5, 0.1)
- phase 4: hand-labeling, held-out precision (0.5, 1.5)
- phase 5: enforce stage, marker line in `rules/workflow.md`, Pi followUp (1.5, 0.5)

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Phases 1-3 done, or consciously dropped at gate G1 (fewer than about 5 measured bad stops per week for Claude Code: keep telemetry only)
- [ ] Per-rule decision recorded: enforce, or retire, with the held-out precision
- [ ] Out of scope: the waiter itself, headless workers, subagent stops
